# The production entrance (specs/141, ADR-003): one host for the storefront, one for the back office, HTTPS for both.
# Caddy obtains and renews the certificates; for *.localhost it uses its own CA, which is how the overlay is verified on
# a laptop. Everything behind it is the apps' nginx, which forwards /api to the gateway - one origin per app, no CORS.

#
# HSTS is set here (specs/151, #294), the one place that speaks HTTPS: a browser that has seen it never tries plain HTTP
# for that host again for a year, so a first-request downgrade cannot strip TLS. Not includeSubDomains and not preload:
# the shop does not own what other names under its domain serve. Caddy's own Server header goes too - the apps' nginx
# sends none with a version, and neither should the entrance. Every other security header is the apps' own.
(security) {
	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		-Server
	}
}

{$SHOP_DOMAIN} {
	import security
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy storefront:8080
}

{$PORTAL_DOMAIN} {
	import security
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy back-office:8080
}
